-- Premières traductions anglaises (Ballon d'Or), traduites depuis les versions françaises publiées.
UPDATE "articles" SET "en_title" = 'Ballon d''Or 2026: Harry Kane crowned the best player in the world', "en_dek" = 'It''s official: ⭐ Harry Kane has won the 2026 Ballon d''Or. At the ceremony at the London Palladium, Bayern Munich''s English striker received the trophy from ⭐ Ronaldo, the Brazilian. He succeeds ⭐ Ousmane Dembélé.', "en_body_html" = '<h2>Harry Kane, the first Englishman to win the Ballon d''Or since 2001</h2><p>England had waited twenty-five years. Since Michael Owen in 2001, no English player had won the Ballon d''Or. Now it has happened, and on home soil: for the first time in its history, the ceremony was held in London, the city where Kane grew up and made his name at Tottenham.</p><p>To present the trophy, the organisers chose a legend: Ronaldo, the Brazilian, a two-time Ballon d''Or winner (1997 and 2002). A powerful symbol: one king of goalscorers crowning another.</p><h2>A record season with Bayern Munich</h2><p>This 2026 Ballon d''Or rewards an exceptional season. With Bayern Munich, Harry Kane scored 36 Bundesliga goals. He won a third straight Bundesliga top scorer title and completed the treble of Bundesliga, German Cup and Super Cup.</p><p>The 2026 World Cup did not bring him the title, but the 100 voting journalists rewarded the consistency of a striker who never stops scoring. Long criticised for his empty trophy cabinet, Kane is now the best player in the world.</p><h2>The full list of 2026 Ballon d''Or winners</h2><ul><li>Men''s Ballon d''Or: ⭐ Harry Kane (Bayern Munich, England)</li><li>Women''s Ballon d''Or: ⭐ Alexia Putellas, the third of her career</li><li>Kopa Trophy (best young player): ⭐ Lamine Yamal, for the third year in a row</li><li>Women''s Kopa Trophy: Vicky López (FC Barcelona)</li><li>Gerd Müller Trophy (top scorer): ⭐ Harry Kane and Charlyn Corral</li><li>Cruyff Trophy (coach of the year): Luis de la Fuente, world champion with Spain</li><li>Best coach of a women''s team: Pere Romeu (FC Barcelona)</li></ul><h2>The highlights of the ceremony in London</h2><p>The 70th Ballon d''Or ceremony started 30 minutes late because of London traffic. A few hours earlier, the official website had mistakenly published three articles announcing three different winners (Kane, Yamal and Mbappé), before taking them down.</p><p>Another standout moment: on receiving his third Kopa Trophy, Lamine Yamal paid tribute to his teammate Pau Cubarsí, who he said deserved the award.</p><h2>The full 2026 Ballon d''Or ranking</h2><p>Who joins Harry Kane on the podium? Where do Kylian Mbappé, Lamine Yamal and Ousmane Dembélé finish? Read the full ranking here: <a href="/en/articles/ballon-d-or-2026-le-classement-complet">Ballon d''Or 2026: the full ranking</a>. ⚽</p>', "en_published" = true
WHERE "slug" = 'ballon-d-or-2026-harry-kane-sacre-meilleur-joueur-du-monde' AND "en_title" = '';--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE "articles" SET "en_title" = 'Ballon d''Or 2026: the full ranking, from Harry Kane to 29th place', "en_dek" = 'Harry Kane ahead of Kylian Mbappé and Lamine Yamal: here are the 30 players ranked in the 2026 Ballon d''Or, with a tie for 29th place.', "en_body_html" = '<p>The London Palladium delivered its verdict on Monday night: ⭐ Harry Kane is the 2026 Ballon d''Or winner. Behind the English striker, Kylian Mbappé and Lamine Yamal complete the podium. Here is the full ranking of the players selected by the jury, from 1st to 29th place, with a tie that explains why there is no 30th.</p><p>The story of the night and the other award winners are here: <a href="/en/articles/ballon-d-or-2026-harry-kane-sacre-meilleur-joueur-du-monde">Harry Kane crowned the best player in the world</a>.</p><h2>The podium</h2><ol start="1"><li>⭐ Harry Kane (Bayern Munich, England)</li><li>Kylian Mbappé (Real Madrid, France)</li><li>Lamine Yamal (FC Barcelona, Spain)</li></ol><h2>4th to 10th place</h2><ol start="4"><li>Rodri (FC Barcelona, Spain)</li><li>Lionel Messi (Inter Miami, Argentina)</li><li>Khvicha Kvaratskhelia (PSG, Georgia)</li><li>Ousmane Dembélé (PSG, France)</li><li>Erling Haaland (Manchester City, Norway)</li><li>Michael Olise (Bayern Munich, France)</li><li>Fabián Ruiz (PSG, Spain)</li></ol><h2>11th to 20th place</h2><ol start="11"><li>Jude Bellingham (Real Madrid, England)</li><li>Pau Cubarsí (FC Barcelona, Spain)</li><li>Achraf Hakimi (PSG, Morocco)</li><li>Vitinha (PSG, Portugal)</li><li>Declan Rice (Arsenal, England)</li><li>Ferran Torres (PSG, Spain)</li><li>Vinícius Júnior (Real Madrid, Brazil)</li><li>Marc Cucurella (Real Madrid, Spain)</li><li>João Neves (PSG, Portugal)</li><li>Willian Pacho (PSG, Ecuador)</li></ol><h2>21st to 29th place</h2><ol start="21"><li>Gabriel (Arsenal, Brazil)</li><li>Lautaro Martínez (Inter Milan, Argentina)</li><li>Nuno Mendes (PSG, Portugal)</li><li>Luis Díaz (Bayern Munich, Colombia)</li><li>Marquinhos (PSG, Brazil)</li><li>Dayot Upamecano (Bayern Munich, France)</li><li>Bruno Fernandes (Manchester United, Portugal)</li><li>Julián Quiñones (Al-Qadsiah, Mexico)</li></ol><ul><li>Joint 29th: William Saliba (Arsenal, France) and Sadio Mané (Al-Nassr, Senegal)</li></ul><p>Ferran Torres and Marc Cucurella have changed clubs since the voting period: they are listed here under their current club.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul><li>PSG have ten players in the ranking, from Kvaratskhelia (6th) to Marquinhos (25th). No other club has as many.</li><li>Ousmane Dembélé, the holder, finishes 7th.</li><li>Lionel Messi is still there: 5th with Inter Miami.</li><li>Our surprise pick, Fabián Ruiz, makes the top 10. Khvicha Kvaratskhelia, who missed the World Cup with Georgia, takes 6th place. Read <a href="/articles/ballon-d-or-2026-le-trone-sans-roi">our pre-ceremony preview</a> (in French).</li><li>Pau Cubarsí, to whom Lamine Yamal dedicated his Kopa Trophy, finishes 12th.</li></ul><h2>Sources</h2><p>Ranking published after the ceremony and checked against three outlets: <a href="https://www.footmercato.net/a7319110063199534207-le-classement-final-du-ballon-dor-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Foot Mercato</a>, <a href="https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/50289067/ballon-dor-2026-results-full-rankings-all-award-winners" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ESPN</a> and <a href="https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/2026-ballon-dor-final-rankings-230119799.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">USA Today / Yahoo Sports</a>. ⚽</p>', "en_published" = true
WHERE "slug" = 'ballon-d-or-2026-le-classement-complet' AND "en_title" = '';
